  "tagline": "Community-maintained continuation of Kùzu: embedded columnar graph database with Cypher.",
  "description": "LadybugDB is the actively maintained fork of Kùzu, created when Kùzu's repository was archived after Apple agreed to acquire its company in October 2025. It keeps the same design: an embedded, in-process property-graph database with columnar disk storage, CSR adjacency indexes, vectorized and factorized execution, serializable ACID transactions, Cypher, and native full-text and vector indexes, plus WebAssembly bindings. It remains MIT licensed and ships frequent releases (0.22.0 in October 2026), sponsored by Ladybug Memory. It is the natural choice for Kùzu users and anyone wanting a DuckDB-style graph database inside their app.",
